   106	What freezing removes and changes (C3I → C3G, same in the C3 → C3G view): the 420 parameter-cast kernels (0.92 ms at 8 s, 0.86 ms at 100 ms) disappear; the rotary cos/sin are folded (the fused SDPA-side signature `…add,cos,mul,sin` is replaced by `…add,mul` at equal time, 1.36 → 1.39 ms at 8 s); the norm+cast kernels shrink by 0.35 ms at 8 s; the launch count falls by 413 per pass. What freezing costs: the GEMM class is slower after freezing, by 0.13 ms at 8 s and by **0.37 ms at 100 ms** — at 100 ms the GEMM slow-down eats 44 % of the cast saving, which is why the device-time class sum (0.48) is well below the unprofiled gain (0.74) and why the 100 ms gain on the reduce-overhead base is smaller than on the other two bases. The remaining gap between the device-time sum and the unprofiled wall gain is consistent with the launch-count reduction priced at the Phase-3 boundary-bench per-node cost of a graph replay (0.57–0.72 µs/node × 413 nodes ≈ 0.24–0.30 ms: 0.48 + 0.24…0.30 ≈ 0.72–0.78 vs 0.74 observed at 100 ms; 1.14 + 0.24…0.30 ≈ 1.38–1.44 vs 1.30 observed at 8 s, inside the restart spread 1.16–1.32). That is a consistency check between independently measured quantities, not a causal split: the unprofiled gain is the primary result and the residual (≈ 0.0 ms at 100 ms, ≈ −0.1 ms at 8 s) is reported, not assigned. Inlining off alone changes almost nothing in device time (+0.06 ms class sum at 8 s; +0.06 ms on the GELU kernel) while costing 0.2 ms of wall time; that wall cost is not visible in the traces and stays unresolved. HG (192 kernels per pass, 0 casts, 64 extern GEMMs) and C3MG (556 kernels, 0 casts, 285 Triton template GEMMs + 15 cuBLAS GEMMs at 8 s; 291 + 14 at 100 ms) are documented as deployed; the comparison with their session-3 controls (H, C3M: 178 templates + 145 extern at 8 s) is cross-session and descriptive only: freezing on the max-autotune base moved most GEMMs from cuBLAS entry points into Triton templates.
