    18	## Statistics, fixed before measuring
    19	- Primary statistic per pair and operating point: median over restarts of the per-restart median of the per-repeat paired difference (a − b of block medians; 5 repeats × 50 passes per restart), with a two-level cluster bootstrap interval (restarts, then repeats; 10,000 draws, seed 20260921). Restart medians and their range are reported beside it (`fullmodel/stats_v2.py`).
    20	- Eligibility: the shared validator (`qualify.pair_problems`), manifest binding, and the registered 5 % clock rule applied per repeat (flagged or clock-unresolved repeats excluded; a stage needs at least one eligible restart with clean repeats). Correctness gates run first: every arm used in a PC pair has its r1 SDR gate at both operating points before its pairs; a FAIL stops that arm (its pairs are recorded UNTESTED) and no speed value is published for it. The standalone C1P run carries the SDR gate in r1.
    21	- Smallest practically meaningful difference (declared now): 0.30 ms at 352,800 / 264,600 / 176,400 and 0.10 ms at 44,100 / 4,410, i.e. about 1 % of the 8 s wall and 4 % of the 100 ms wall. A pair is reported as: "a faster" or "b faster" when the interval excludes zero and |point| ≥ the threshold; "practical tie" when the interval lies within ±threshold; "unresolved" otherwise. No measurement is repeated to reach a preferred outcome; the repetition schedule is fixed above.
    22	- Ranking claims are per measured length only; no crossover location is interpolated between lengths.
    23	- Order policy: within a matched process the control arm is built first and blocks alternate a, b, a, b, …; the same policy applies to the A/A control, which measures order/position bias. PB additionally swaps the build order for C1/C1P to test the build-order interaction directly.
    24	
