docs/phase4/revision/analysis_revision.md:7:- Corrected reading: with unit tile factors the model is exactly affine in frames, D(F) = 1.136476 − 0.001915801·F ms (`docs/phase4/e9_affine_check.json`). Its four calibration residuals (+0.18, +0.14, −0.42, +0.09 ms) come from fitting a line to non-monotone values; a different line meets the 0.4 ms tolerance on those values (max 0.288 ms), so the miss is not an inevitability of affine forms. Three things are confounded in the held-out miss and are not separated by the evidence: the representational restriction (a line), the fitted coefficients (sweep refit with soft trace constraints), and transfer to another physical card and session. The Phase-3 sentence "the fixed terms transfer and the efficiency term does not" is withdrawn: `e9_residual.json` shows only that changing one rate would absorb the residual, which is sensitivity, not attribution. E9 remains a failed registered test; nothing is refitted.
docs/phase4/revision/analysis_revision.md:8:- Retrospective comparators recorded for any future predictor work (labelled retrospective): the calibration-only minimax line; a piecewise-linear interpolation through the four sweep points gives +0.616 ms at 176,400 and +0.062 ms at 264,600 (closer to the observations than the registered line, but selected after seeing them, so it is not a validated predictor).
docs/phase4/revision/analysis_revision.md:13:- The 100 ms A/A control missed its 0.05 ms threshold (−0.058 ms) with an interval including zero; every 100 ms claim carries that, plus the registered clock rule's flags (three 100 ms headline cells of session 3 clock-flagged; flagged repeats excluded from pair aggregates).
docs/phase4/revision/analysis_revision.md:38:- **§1/§3 (E9, provenance, crossover):** on one GPU, matched C3 − H = +1.512 [1.499, 1.540] at 1 s, +0.846 [0.829, 0.922] at 4 s, +0.455 [0.318, 0.601] at 6 s (H faster; thresholds 0.10/0.30/0.30) and −0.331 [−0.389, −0.232] at 8 s (C3 faster by the registered rule — interval excludes zero, |point| ≥ 0.30 — with a thin margin over the threshold). A/A controls: practical ties at all five lengths. The stored affine predictor mis-predicts by ≈ 0.5 ms at 1/4/6 s (sign wrong at 6 s) and by 0.07 ms at 8 s (`docs/phase4/e9_retrospective_session4.json`); E9's registered verdict stays FAIL and nothing is refitted. The direction at 4 s and 6 s replicates the Phase-3 pairs on another GPU; the 8 s pairing is a third labelled observation next to Sep-20 (H slower by 0.495) and the unpaired session-3 summaries. No crossover length is claimed.
docs/phase4/revision/analysis_revision.md:39:- **§6 (C1P):** the +15 ms matched-context penalty is a build-order artefact of the matched runner: standalone unprofiled C1P = 36.36–36.80 ms with the SDR gate PASS (equal to C1); matched C1→C1P −15.259 [−15.299, −15.219]; matched C1P→C1 −15.220 [−15.291, −15.167] — the second-built arm is the slow one whichever it is. The profiled matched process shows the 15.4 ms as 14.6 ms of GPU-busy time (215 more kernels, 51 vs 96 graph launches), not host time; the torch logs of both build orders (never the standalone runs) show dynamo's recompile limit exhausted on the attention `forward` frame in the second build, after which that frame runs eager. §6's "not supported" clause (host-side reading) is now refuted; the mechanism is supported by logs and composition, not by intervention.
docs/phase4/revision/analysis_revision.md:40:- **§5 (freezing beyond casts):** with inlining off, freezing gains +1.296 [1.145, 1.369] at 8 s and +0.743 [0.740, 0.750] at 100 ms (C3I → C3G); inlining off alone costs −0.206 [−0.329, −0.049] / −0.084 [−0.094, −0.062] (below thresholds, consistent sign). Traces: casts 0.92/0.86 ms removed, rotary cos/sin folded at equal time, norm+cast kernels −0.35 ms at 8 s, 413 fewer launches, GEMM class −0.13 (8 s) / −0.37 ms (100 ms) slower after freezing. The device-time class sums (1.14 / 0.48) plus the launch reduction priced at the Phase-3 per-node graph cost (0.24–0.30 ms) match the unprofiled gains within the restart spread; reported as a consistency check, not a causal split.
docs/phase4/revision/analysis_revision.md:42:- **Statistics (§2):** every session-4 verdict uses the declared primary statistic and its cluster-bootstrap interval; the historical pooled interval is stored alongside and never used for a verdict; with three restarts the interval is the restart-median spread (stated in each record).
SESSION4_RESULT.md:4:Conventions: matched differences are first − second arm in ms (+ = second arm faster); point = median over eligible restarts of per-restart medians of per-repeat block-median differences; interval = two-level cluster bootstrap (restarts, then repeats; 10,000 draws, seed 20260921); clock-flagged repeats excluded; restart medians shown. Practical thresholds (declared in advance): {352800: 0.3, 264600: 0.3, 176400: 0.3, 44100: 0.1, 4410: 0.1} ms. Verdict rule: 'x faster' needs the interval to exclude zero and |point| ≥ threshold; 'practical tie' needs the interval inside ±threshold.
