docs/phase4/EXPERIMENT_REPORT_session4.md:79:Reading, without adding gains. (i) Turning inlining off by itself does not help: −0.2 ms at 8 s and −0.08 ms at 100 ms, both below threshold but consistent in sign. (ii) Freezing, with inlining off, is the effect: +1.30 ms at 8 s and +0.74 ms at 100 ms on the reduce-overhead base. (iii) The same freezing + no-inlining change is worth +1.31 ms on the max-autotune base and +1.36 ms on the pad-and-batch base at 8 s, and +1.03 / +1.03 ms at 100 ms. At 8 s the gain is of one size on three bases; at 100 ms the reduce-overhead base gains less (0.74) than the other two (1.03). PC3 and PC4 measure their compositions directly; nothing is summed. Standalone context (r1 min-of-medians, same session, unpaired): at 8 s C3 29.79, C3I 29.89, C3G 28.56, C3M 24.80, **C3MG 23.56**, H 30.11, HG 28.73, C1P 36.38 ms; at 100 ms C3 3.50, C3I 3.57, C3G 2.83, C3M 3.36, C3MG 2.25, H 2.44, **HG 1.39** ms.
docs/phase4/EXPERIMENT_REPORT_session4.md:106:What freezing removes and changes (C3I → C3G, same in the C3 → C3G view): the 420 parameter-cast kernels (0.92 ms at 8 s, 0.86 ms at 100 ms) disappear; the rotary cos/sin are folded (the fused SDPA-side signature `…add,cos,mul,sin` is replaced by `…add,mul` at equal time, 1.36 → 1.39 ms at 8 s); the norm+cast kernels shrink by 0.35 ms at 8 s; the launch count falls by 413 per pass. What freezing costs: the GEMM class is slower after freezing, by 0.13 ms at 8 s and by **0.37 ms at 100 ms** — at 100 ms the GEMM slow-down eats 44 % of the cast saving, which is why the device-time class sum (0.48) is well below the unprofiled gain (0.74) and why the 100 ms gain on the reduce-overhead base is smaller than on the other two bases. The remaining gap between the device-time sum and the unprofiled wall gain is consistent with the launch-count reduction priced at the Phase-3 boundary-bench per-node cost of a graph replay (0.57–0.72 µs/node × 413 nodes ≈ 0.24–0.30 ms: 0.48 + 0.24…0.30 ≈ 0.72–0.78 vs 0.74 observed at 100 ms; 1.14 + 0.24…0.30 ≈ 1.38–1.44 vs 1.30 observed at 8 s, inside the restart spread 1.16–1.32). That is a consistency check between independently measured quantities, not a causal split: the unprofiled gain is the primary result and the residual (≈ 0.0 ms at 100 ms, ≈ −0.1 ms at 8 s) is reported, not assigned. Inlining off alone changes almost nothing in device time (+0.06 ms class sum at 8 s; +0.06 ms on the GELU kernel) while costing 0.2 ms of wall time; that wall cost is not visible in the traces and stays unresolved. HG (192 kernels per pass, 0 casts, 64 extern GEMMs) and C3MG (556 kernels, 0 casts, 285 Triton template GEMMs + 15 cuBLAS GEMMs at 8 s; 291 + 14 at 100 ms) are documented as deployed; the comparison with their session-3 controls (H, C3M: 178 templates + 145 extern at 8 s) is cross-session and descriptive only: freezing on the max-autotune base moved most GEMMs from cuBLAS entry points into Triton templates.
docs/phase4/EXPERIMENT_REPORT_session4.md:119:The predictor under-estimates H's advantage by ≈ 0.5 ms at every length below 8 s on this GPU, exactly as it did on the Phase-3 GPU (failed held-out test), and gets the sign wrong at 6 s. This is a retrospective comparison on a third GPU; 4 s / 6 s were the Phase-3 held-out points and 8 s / 100 ms its calibration points, so nothing here validates a model out of sample.
docs/phase4/EXPERIMENT_REPORT_session4.md:126:- The 8 s PA verdict "C3 faster" rests on |point| = 0.331 vs the 0.30 ms threshold with restart medians 0.297–0.332; the margin over the declared threshold is thin and is stated as such.
docs/phase4/EXPERIMENT_REPORT_session4.md:127:- PC1 at 8 s is "unresolved" (interval [−0.33, −0.05]); the sign is consistent.
docs/phase4/EXPERIMENT_REPORT_session4.md:135:**Observed effects (direct, matched, same GPU):** H faster than C3 at 1 s (+1.51 ms), 4 s (+0.85) and 6 s (+0.45); C3 faster at 8 s (−0.33, registered rule met with a thin margin over the 0.30 ms threshold). The 15 ms "C1P regression" is a build-order artefact of the matched runner (−15.26 with C1 first, −15.22 with C1P first; standalone C1P = C1). Freezing with inlining off gains +1.30 (8 s) / +0.74 (100 ms) on reduce-overhead, +1.31 / +1.03 on max-autotune, +1.36 / +1.03 on pad-and-batch; inlining off alone costs 0.2 / 0.08 ms. All new arms are numerically valid, fully graphed and pass the SDR gate.
docs/phase4/EXPERIMENT_REPORT_session4.md:137:**Explanations supported by discriminating evidence:** the second-built arm's slow-down is GPU-busy time from an eager attention forward after dynamo's recompile limit is exhausted (logs in both orders, never standalone; profiled composition). Freezing's gain comes with the removal of the 420 parameter casts, rotary folding, norm+cast shrinkage and 413 fewer launches, and against a GEMM-class slow-down that is largest at 100 ms (−0.37 ms), which explains the base dependence at 100 ms.

