106 The remaining gap between the device-time sum and the unprofiled wall gain is consistent with the launch-count reduction priced at the Phase-3 boundary-bench per-node cost of a graph replay (0.57–0.72 µs/node × 413 nodes ≈ 0.24–0.30 ms: 0.48 + 0.24…0.30 ≈ 0.72–0.78 vs 0.74 observed at 100 ms; 1.14 + 0.24…0.30 ≈ 1.38–1.44 vs 1.30 observed at 8 s, inside the restart spread 1.16–1.32). That is a consistency check between independently measured quantities, not a causal split: the unprofiled gain is the primary result and the residual (≈ 0.0 ms at 100 ms, ≈ −0.1 ms at 8 s) is reported, not assigned. Inlining off alone changes almost nothing in device time (+0.06 ms class sum at 8 s; +0.06 ms on the GELU kernel) while costing 0.2 ms of wall time; that wall cost is not visible in the traces and stays unresolved. HG (192 kernels per pass, 0 casts, 64 extern GEMMs) and C3MG (556 kernels, 0 casts, 285 Triton template GEMMs + 15 cuBLAS GEMMs at 8 
