39 - **§6 (C1P):** the +15 ms matched-context penalty is a build-order artefact of the matched runner: standalone unprofiled C1P = 36.36–36.80 ms with the SDR gate PASS (equal to C1); matched C1→C1P −15.259 [−15.299, −15.219]; matched C1P→C1 −15.220 [−15.291, −15.167] — the second-built arm is the slow one whichever it is. The profiled matched process shows the 15.4 ms as 14.6 ms of GPU-busy time (215 more kernels, 51 vs 96 graph launches), not host time; the torch logs of both build orders (never the standalone runs) show dynamo's recompile limit exhausted on the attention `forward` frame in the second build, after which that frame runs eager. §6's "not supported" clause (host-side reading) is now refuted; the mechanism is supported by logs and composition, not by intervention.
40 - **§5 (freezing beyond casts):** with inlining off, freezing gains +1.296 [1.145, 1.369] at 8 s and +0.743 [0.740, 0.750] at 100 ms (C3I → C3G); inlining off alone costs −0.206 [−0.329, −0.049] / −0.084 [−0.094, −0.062] (below thresholds, consistent sign). Traces: casts 0.92/0.86 ms removed, rotary cos/sin folded at equal time, norm+cast kernels −0.35 ms at 8 s, 413 fewer launches, GEMM class −0.13 (8 s) / −0.37 ms (100 ms) slower after freezing. The device-time class sums (1.14 / 0.48) plus the launch reduction priced at the Phase-3 per-node graph cost (0.24–0.30 ms) match the unprofiled gains within the restart spread; reported as a consistency check, not a causal split.
