170. **MINOR — [EXPERIMENT_REPORT_session4.md:36](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/docs/phase4/EXPERIMENT_REPORT_session4.md:36), [analysis_revision.md:42](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/docs/phase4/revision/analysis_revision.md:42): bootstrap intervals are misdescribed as restart-median spreads.** For PC1 at 8 s, the restart range is **[−0.213627, −0.153879]**, while the correctly computed interval is **[−0.329075, −0.049406]**. Repeat resampling contributes uncertainty. The same misleading sentence appears in the JSON’s `inference_scope`, including one- and two-restart cases. **Minimal fix:** describe limited restart information without equating the interval to the range; state the actual restart count.

